---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactInvite from '../components/ContactInvite.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<Base title="Studio"
  ><div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">ExoSquare</div><h1>
        An independent idea and<br />experimental technology studio.
      </h1><p>{site.framing}</p>
    </header><section class="editorial-grid studio-section">
      <h2>What brings us here</h2><div class="prose">
        <p class="studio-statement">
          Software becomes meaningful when people use it.
        </p><p>
          We build software and explore questions about technology through
          experiments and writing. The work is a place to show the thinking,
          evidence, and lessons alongside the result.
        </p><p>
          Some questions lead to useful systems. Others change what we try next.
          Both deserve a careful record.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section><section class="editorial-grid studio-section">
      <h2>How we work</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          We value room to explore, clear context, and thoughtful
          follow-through. People should be able to ask questions, test an idea,
          and say when they do not know.
        </p><p>
          Project records make room for what failed and what changed. Claims
          about results belong with the evidence that supports them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section><section id="matt" class="editorial-grid studio-section">
      <h2>About Matt</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>Matt convenes ExoSquare and writes about the software experiments documented here. His posts describe what he tried, what happened and what he would investigate next.</p>
        <p><a href="../writing/">Read the experiment notes</a> or <a href="../contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section><section id="editorial" class="editorial-grid studio-section">
      <h2>Editorial approach</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>Experiment notes distinguish observations, external documentation and interpretation. A small trial can reveal a useful failure without establishing a general accuracy rate. Where a result depends on a particular setup, the note describes that setup and its limits.</p>
        <p>Questions and corrections are welcome through the <a href="../contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section><ContactInvite />
  </div></Base
>
